<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Br J Cancer</journal-id><journal-title>British Journal of Cancer</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0007-0920</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1532-1827</issn></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">1212410</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2024760</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Research Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Colorectal cancer and consumption of beef and fat.</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Enstrom</surname><given-names>J. E.</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><month>10</month><year>1975</year></pub-date><volume>32</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>432</fpage><lpage>439</lpage><abstract><p>Secular, socioeconomic and urban-rural gradients and geographical differences in beef and fat consumption within the United States of America are compared with corresponding data on colorectal cancer incidence and mortality rates. These results, together with the results of most previous epidemiological studies, appear to contradict the hypothesis that beef and fat consumption are involved in the aetiology of colorectal cancer.</p></abstract></article-meta></front><body><supplementary-material content-type="scanned-pages"><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00319-0024.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="432" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00319-0025.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="433" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00319-0026.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="434" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00319-0027.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="435" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00319-0028.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="436" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00319-0029.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="437" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00319-0030.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="438" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00319-0031.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="439" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/></supplementary-material></body></article>